# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT NEVER GOES TO GITHUB.
#
# ---- READ THIS BEFORE YOU LOOSEN ANYTHING BELOW ----
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Gigi's call, Aug 24 2026.
#
# And git is not like the Netlify near-miss at v3.72, where a file could be
# taken back out of `public/` and the problem was over. GIT KEEPS HISTORY.
# Committing a file once and deleting it in the next commit does NOT remove it:
# it stays in the repository for ever, in every clone anyone has ever made, and
# a public repo is scraped by machines within hours of being pushed.
#
# So the rule for this file is stricter than for `public/`:
#
#   IF IT NAMES AZIANNA OR MEASURES HER, IT DOES NOT GO IN.
#
# `check-publish-safety` asserts the rules below rather than trusting them.
# Deleting a line here will fail the build, on purpose. If you mean to change
# one, change the check too, and write down why and when — the same way every
# other reversal in this project is recorded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---- HER DATA. THE WHOLE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS. -------------------------
#
# Each of these parses as a full export: her learner name, all nine measured
# strand levels, 74 answers, and both journal entries in her own words.
#
# There were THIRTEEN copies of it in this folder on Aug 24 2026.

local/
*her-latest-export*.json
*her-backup*.json
her-*.json

# The scratch copies from v3.72's negative tests — eleven of them. This folder
# is meant to be moved out of the project entirely; the ignore is the belt as
# well as the braces.
_to_delete/
_to_delete-from-app/
_archive-test/


# ---- HER RECORDS AND THE PROJECT'S NOTES ---------------------------------
#
# ⚠️ `claude/` IS NOT DOCUMENTATION. It holds `azianna-diagnostic-results.md`,
# which is a full educational assessment of a named nine-year-old — every
# measured strand level, the item-level detail behind them, and how often she
# needed a question read aloud. Her name appears across about thirty files in
# there, and `her-backup-2026-08-18.json` is her raw record.
#
# The master plan and the build log are the best writing in this project and it
# is a real loss to leave them out. They also quote her name and her levels on
# 27 lines between them.
#
# TO PUBLISH THEM ANYWAY: delete the `claude/` line, and update
# `check-publish-safety` — it fails if this line is missing, deliberately, so
# that publishing a child's assessment is a decision somebody makes on purpose
# rather than something that happens because a line was tidied away.

claude/


# ---- BUILD OUTPUT --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Netlify runs `npm run build` itself, so `dist/` is made fresh on their
# machine from the committed source. Committing it means the site and the code
# can silently disagree about which version is live — and `dist/` has carried
# her export before (v3.72).

dist/
node_modules/
.vite/
*.local


# ---- ENVIRONMENT AND EDITOR ----------------------------------------------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
